WEBVTT

00:00.514 --> 00:01.714
- [Voiceover] What we
want to do is find the

00:01.714 --> 00:03.103
derivative of this G of X

00:03.103 --> 00:04.518
and at first it can look intimidating.

00:04.518 --> 00:05.584
We have a sine of X here.

00:05.584 --> 00:06.754
We have a cosine of X.

00:06.754 --> 00:09.102
We have this crazy expression here

00:09.102 --> 00:10.892
with a pi over cube root of X

00:10.892 --> 00:12.022
we're squaring the whole thing

00:12.022 --> 00:13.558
and at first it might seem intimidating.

00:13.558 --> 00:14.945
But as we'll see in this video, we can

00:14.945 --> 00:17.717
actually do this with the
tools already in our tool kit.

00:17.717 --> 00:20.007
Using our existing derivative properties

00:20.007 --> 00:21.953
using what we know about the power rule

00:21.953 --> 00:25.184
which tells us the
derivative with respect to X.

00:25.184 --> 00:26.267
Of X to the N

00:27.499 --> 00:29.166
is equal to N

00:29.166 --> 00:30.953
times X to the N minus one,

00:30.953 --> 00:32.558
we've see that multiple times.

00:32.558 --> 00:34.957
We also need to use the fact

00:34.957 --> 00:37.767
that the derivative of cosine of X

00:37.767 --> 00:40.035
is equal to negative the sine of X.

00:40.035 --> 00:41.449
And the other way around

00:41.449 --> 00:44.116
the derivative with respect to X

00:45.573 --> 00:47.035
of sine of X

00:47.035 --> 00:49.293
is equal to positive

00:49.293 --> 00:50.572
cosine of X.

00:50.572 --> 00:53.144
So using just that we can
actually evaluate this.

00:53.144 --> 00:55.291
Or evaluate G prime of X.

00:55.291 --> 00:57.880
So, pause the video and
see if you can do it.

00:57.880 --> 01:00.057
So probably the most
intimidating part of this

01:00.057 --> 01:01.643
because we know the derivative's a sine

01:01.643 --> 01:03.916
of X and cosine of X is
this expression here.

01:03.916 --> 01:05.844
And we can just rewrite this

01:05.844 --> 01:07.791
or simplify it a little
bit so it takes a form

01:07.791 --> 01:10.074
that you might be a little
bit more familiar with.

01:10.074 --> 01:12.225
So, so let me just do this

01:12.225 --> 01:13.713
on the side here.

01:13.713 --> 01:14.546
So, pi

01:15.684 --> 01:16.517
pi over

01:17.510 --> 01:19.010
the cube root of X

01:20.274 --> 01:21.506
squared.

01:21.506 --> 01:23.025
Well that's the same thing.

01:23.025 --> 01:25.275
This is equal to pi squared

01:26.174 --> 01:28.841
over the cube root of X squared.

01:30.342 --> 01:31.755
This is just exponent properties

01:31.755 --> 01:33.260
that we're dealing with.

01:33.260 --> 01:35.264
And so this is the same thing.

01:35.264 --> 01:37.470
We're gonna take X to the one third power

01:37.470 --> 01:39.949
and then raise that to the second power.

01:39.949 --> 01:42.780
So this is equal to pi squared

01:42.780 --> 01:44.166
over.

01:44.166 --> 01:44.999
Let me write it this way,

01:44.999 --> 01:45.981
I'm not gonna skip any steps

01:45.981 --> 01:48.387
because this is a good
review of exponent property.

01:48.387 --> 01:50.285
X to the one third squared.

01:50.285 --> 01:53.399
Which is the same thing as pi squared

01:53.399 --> 01:56.684
over X to the two thirds power.

01:56.684 --> 02:00.548
Which is the same thing as pi squared

02:00.548 --> 02:04.069
times X to the negative two thirds power.

02:04.069 --> 02:05.151
So when you write it like this

02:05.151 --> 02:06.681
it starts to get into a formula,

02:06.681 --> 02:08.448
you're like, oh, I can
see how the power rule

02:08.448 --> 02:09.366
could apply there.

02:09.366 --> 02:11.764
So this thing is just pi squared

02:11.764 --> 02:14.681
times X to the negative two thirds power.

02:14.681 --> 02:17.167
So actually let me delete this.

02:17.167 --> 02:18.330
So,

02:18.330 --> 02:19.163
this thing

02:20.746 --> 02:22.163
can be rewritten.

02:23.430 --> 02:24.831
This thing can be rewritten

02:24.831 --> 02:25.914
as pi squared

02:27.261 --> 02:29.178
times X to the negative

02:30.242 --> 02:32.992
to the negative two thirds power.

02:33.830 --> 02:35.022
So now let's take the derivative

02:35.022 --> 02:38.944
of each of these pieces
of this expression.

02:38.944 --> 02:40.505
So, we're gonna take

02:40.505 --> 02:43.585
we want to evaluate what
the G prime of X is.

02:43.585 --> 02:44.835
So G prime of X

02:45.766 --> 02:47.353
is going to be equal to.

02:47.353 --> 02:48.785
You could view it as a
derivative with respect

02:48.785 --> 02:51.570
to X of seven sine of X.

02:51.570 --> 02:52.562
So

02:52.562 --> 02:54.930
we can take do the derivative operator

02:54.930 --> 02:56.569
on both sides here just to make it clear

02:56.569 --> 02:57.977
what we're doing.

02:57.977 --> 02:59.490
So we're gonna apply it there.

02:59.490 --> 03:02.173
We're gonna apply it there.

03:02.173 --> 03:04.037
And we're going to apply it

03:04.037 --> 03:05.614
there.

03:05.614 --> 03:07.099
So this derivative

03:07.099 --> 03:09.347
this is the same thing as

03:09.347 --> 03:12.369
this is going to be seven
times the derivative

03:12.369 --> 03:13.878
of sine of X.

03:13.878 --> 03:16.215
So this is just gonna be seven times

03:16.215 --> 03:17.215
cosine of X.

03:19.227 --> 03:21.342
This one, over here,

03:21.342 --> 03:23.689
this is gonna be three,
or we're subtracting,

03:23.689 --> 03:25.402
so it's gonna be this subtract

03:25.402 --> 03:26.235
this minus.

03:26.235 --> 03:28.591
We can bring the constant out

03:28.591 --> 03:30.802
that we're multiplying the expression by.

03:30.802 --> 03:33.202
And the derivative of cosine of X

03:33.202 --> 03:35.255
so it's minus three times

03:35.255 --> 03:37.035
the derivative of cosine of X

03:37.035 --> 03:39.311
is negative sine of X.

03:39.311 --> 03:40.894
Negative sine of X.

03:42.131 --> 03:44.165
And then finally

03:44.165 --> 03:46.852
here in the yellow we
just apply the power rule.

03:46.852 --> 03:49.230
So, we have the negative two thirds,

03:49.230 --> 03:50.666
actually, let's not forget this minus sign

03:50.666 --> 03:52.108
I'm gonna write it out here.

03:52.108 --> 03:53.264
So you have the negative two thirds.

03:53.264 --> 03:55.566
You multiply the exponent
times the coefficient.

03:55.566 --> 03:56.876
It might look confusing, pi squared,

03:56.876 --> 03:58.054
but that's just a number.

03:58.054 --> 03:59.265
So it's gonna be

03:59.265 --> 04:00.136
negative

04:00.136 --> 04:02.410
and then you have negative two thirds

04:02.410 --> 04:03.827
times pi squared.

04:04.673 --> 04:06.090
Times pi squared.

04:07.023 --> 04:09.591
Times X to the negative two thirds

04:09.591 --> 04:11.017
minus one power.

04:11.017 --> 04:12.591
Negative two thirds

04:12.591 --> 04:13.922
minus one power.

04:13.922 --> 04:15.634
So what is this going to be?

04:15.634 --> 04:17.467
So we get G prime of X

04:18.792 --> 04:19.709
is equal to

04:20.762 --> 04:21.906
is equal to

04:21.906 --> 04:23.406
seven cosine of X.

04:24.827 --> 04:26.344
And let's see, we have a negative three

04:26.344 --> 04:27.829
times a negative sine of X.

04:27.829 --> 04:30.912
So that's a positive three sine of X.

04:32.550 --> 04:34.061
And then

04:34.061 --> 04:35.477
we have, we're subtracting

04:35.477 --> 04:36.771
but then this is going to be a negative,

04:36.771 --> 04:38.376
so that's going to be a positive.

04:38.376 --> 04:39.679
So we can say

04:39.679 --> 04:42.262
plus two pi squared over three.

04:43.461 --> 04:46.223
Two pi squared over three.

04:46.223 --> 04:47.744
That's that part there.

04:47.744 --> 04:48.577
Times X

04:49.957 --> 04:51.392
to the.

04:51.392 --> 04:52.747
So negative two thirds

04:52.747 --> 04:53.580
minus one,

04:54.723 --> 04:56.126
we could say negative one and two thirds,

04:56.126 --> 04:59.261
or we could say negative
five thirds by power.

04:59.261 --> 05:02.090
Negative five thirds power.

05:02.090 --> 05:02.923
And there you have it.

05:02.923 --> 05:04.006
We were able to tackle this thing that

05:04.006 --> 05:04.941
looked a little bit hairy

05:04.941 --> 05:07.158
but all we had to use was the power rule

05:07.158 --> 05:09.445
and what we knew to be the derivatives

05:09.445 --> 05:11.028
of sine and cosine.
